From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sweet: add NativeAdreno ABI v2 bridge

Expose UniXNU's fixed-size NativeAdreno ABI through the existing
IOAcceleratorES user client when it is opened with type 0x4147.  The old
SweetMetal scalar selectors remain byte-for-byte compatible.

The bridge keeps per-client ownership for contiguous BOs, maps client-chosen
IOVAs in a dedicated 128-256 GB window, exposes CPU-map leases and metadata,
and submits indirect buffers through the same synchronous CP path already
proven by the display blitter.  Hardware imports are deliberately not
advertised until IOSurface task-page pinning is implemented.

A separate sweetadreno=1 boot switch publishes the service without publishing
MetalPluginName, so the NativeAdreno path can be tested while CoreAnimation
continues to use its working CPU renderer.
